  "title": "Davenport's constant",
  "statement": {
    "representation": "markdown-latex",
    "text": "For a finite (additive) abelian group $G$, the Davenport constant of $G$, denoted $s(G)$, is the smallest integer $t$ so that every sequence of elements of $G$ with length $\\ge t$ has a nontrivial subsequence which sums to zero.\n\nConjecture $s( {\\mathbb Z}_n^d) = d(n-1) + 1$",
